<title>USA: Giddings evaluating alternatives.</title>
<headline>Giddings evaluating alternatives.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Giddings &amp; Lewis Inc said on Tuesday that its board is evaluating the company's strategic alternatives.</p>
<p>It also said it expects to report favorable second quarter results.</p>
<p>In a letter Giddings &amp; Lewis sent to Harnischfeger Industries Inc chairman and chief executive officer Jeffery Grade, the company said a review of its alternatives is in the best interests of its shareholders, customers and employees and that the review is not hurting the company's value.  </p>
<p>Harnischfeger earlier extended a $19 a share tender offer for Giddings &amp; Lewis through May 30. Giddings has rejected Harnischeger's offer, calling it inadequate.</p>
<p>In last year's second quarter, Giddings &amp; Lewis reported sales of $199.6 million and net income of $9.3 million, or $0.27 a share.</p>
